
How to remake the execuatble 
>s_cgroup 
>make


How to run 
>s_cgroup 
> ./MakeCamera /DataAnalysis/MakeThingsPretty/Images.txt /cedar/

images are created in ../Images


Next meeting checklist

1. Rebuild in the ROOT environment:
>s_cgroup
>make clean
>make

2. Make an image-list file with one row per requested plot:
Output,Title,Histogram,File,Zaxis

For LMCE simulations, add 16 rows like:
LMCE01,LMCE_Simulation_01,<histogram name>,<full path to ROOT file>,PE

The existing triggered-event example is:
Triggered20PE,Single_triggered_pixel_above_20_PE,PreN20250424-F04:21-E0TH2F,/storage/hive/project/phy-otte/sstepanoff3/event_cleaning/OutputRank8test/EventCleanedCluster20250424_TC_481_TB_239_NP_481_s_256_FA_800_mp_1_er_100_tr_1.root,PE

3. Run the plotter:
> ./MakeCamera /DataAnalysis/MakeThingsPretty/<your image-list file>.txt /cedar/

The plotter flips every histogram in both camera axes, so sky is on top and the left/right orientation is mirrored too. It puts Ground below Sky and does not draw a compass key.
